From: OHOS SPDK port
Subject: [PATCH] Advance the unit clock for the delayed authentication disconnect

The v25.05 implementation schedules Failure1 disconnects after 100ms, while
the unit tests still expect the final error state immediately after recv.
Drive the real poller using the existing mock clock. All original protocol,
message, and final-state assertions remain unchanged; no state is forced.

--- a/test/unit/lib/nvmf/auth.c/auth_ut.c
+++ b/test/unit/lib/nvmf/auth.c/auth_ut.c
@@ -112,6 +112,20 @@
 #define ut_prep_send_cmd(req, cmd, buf, len) ut_prep_cmd(req, cmd, buf, len, tl)
 #define ut_prep_recv_cmd(req, cmd, buf, len) ut_prep_cmd(req, cmd, buf, len, al)
 
+/* Failure1 responses intentionally disconnect after a delay. Drive the
+ * existing mock clock and real poller before checking the final state.
+ * The protocol assertions below are unchanged.
+ */
+static void
+ut_auth_recv_exec(struct spdk_nvmf_request *req)
+{
+	nvmf_auth_recv_exec(req);
+	if (req->qpair->auth->state == NVMF_QPAIR_AUTH_FAILURE1) {
+		spdk_delay_us(NVMF_AUTH_FAILURE1_DELAY_US);
+		poll_threads();
+	}
+}
+
 static void
 test_auth_send_recv_error(void)
 {
